Repair the complete source below. Rectangles use integer, half-open bounds: `[x, x + width)` by `[y, y + height)`. `Solution.visibleRegion(Rectangle content, Rectangle viewport)` returns their intersection as a new immutable `Rectangle`. Null arguments, negative dimensions, or coordinate sums outside the `int` range must throw `IllegalArgumentException`. Touching or disjoint rectangles return an empty rectangle positioned at the clamped intersection origin. Inputs are immutable and must not be retained. Return a corrected complete `Solution.java` file.

```java
public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {}

    public static final class Rectangle {
        public final int x;
        public final int y;
        public final int width;
        public final int height;

        public Rectangle(int x, int y, int width, int height) {
            if (width < 0 || height < 0
                    || (long) x + width > Integer.MAX_VALUE
                    || (long) x + width < Integer.MIN_VALUE
                    || (long) y + height > Integer.MAX_VALUE
                    || (long) y + height < Integer.MIN_VALUE) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid rectangle");
            }
            this.x = x;
            this.y = y;
            this.width = width;
            this.height = height;
        }
    }

    public static Rectangle visibleRegion(Rectangle content, Rectangle viewport) {
        if (content == null || viewport == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Rectangle is null");
        }
        int left = Math.max(content.x, viewport.x);
        int top = Math.max(content.y, viewport.y);
        int right = Math.max(content.x + content.width, viewport.x + viewport.width);
        int bottom = Math.min(content.y + content.height, viewport.y + viewport.height);
        return new Rectangle(left, top, Math.max(0, right - left),
                Math.max(0, bottom - top));
    }
}
```

